# Text files are stored with LF endings in the repository and checked out with
# LF endings on every platform.  This project is developed on several
# operating systems, and without this a Windows checkout (`core.autocrlf=true`)
# converts LF to CRLF on disk; a later write that preserves the existing
# ending then produces CRLFCRLF, which Python reads as *two* newlines per
# line and which silently corrupts every embedded template string.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary payloads are never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.webm binary
*.mcap binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.whl binary

# Lock files carry no meaningful line endings and are large.
package-lock.json -diff
uv.lock -diff
